14_GCUDAWorker:
---------------

15_GMPIConsumer:
----------------

This example shows how the MPI consumer can be used directly without using GOptimizer.
Usually using GOptimizer is recommended, but this example serves as a demonstration of direct interaction with the consumer framework and
is similar to the example 06_GDirectEA. If you would like to explore the MPI-Consumer with GOptimizer, you can use the
quickstart in ../quickstart and call the executable with --help --showAll to explore all options.

16_GMPISubClients:
------------------

This example shares the evaluation of one individual among several MPI processes. It uses
courtier's MPI cascade (GMPICascade): rank 0 runs the optimization through GOptimizer, the other
processes form groups of a lead (a client of the MPI consumer) and its members (sub-clients),
and each lead evaluates an individual in a round of its group.

17_GAlgorithmChaining:
----------------------

Shows how several optimization algorithms are chained in a single run, each
one handed the best individuals its predecessor found.

18_GLoadableIndividual:
-----------------------

The reference example for a runtime-loadable optimization problem: the problem
is built as a module and a generic optimizer with nothing compiled in loads it
with --individual.

19_GFunctionGPU:
----------------

A stock library individual evaluated on the GPU purely by selecting the GPU
consumer (--consumer gpu). Requires a CUDA device.

20_GLoadableOA:
---------------

The same story one level up: a runtime-loadable optimization ALGORITHM, loaded
with --module by an optimizer that has no algorithm compiled in.

21_GLoadableGPU:
----------------

One loadable module carrying both an individual and its GPU marshaller, run on
the device by a generic optimizer. Requires a CUDA device.


Please check each directory's README for further information. The main source
code file (named similar to the directory it is in) might also prove useful.

Many of the examples are also described in detail in the Geneva manual, see
http://www.gemfony.eu/fileadmin/documentation/geneva-manual.pdf

Compilation
===========

All the examples in this folder are compiled as part of the Geneva tree when it is
configured with GEM_BUILD_EXAMPLES=TRUE; they use targets of the tree and cannot
be built on their own. A project that builds against an installed Geneva starts
from ../quickstart, whose README shows the steps.
